  "note": "Triennial election of the electoral divisions of Lisnaskea rural district, one member each, polled on 2 June 1949. Two divisions were contested, Newtownbutler and Mullynagoan, both won by Unionists from Anti-Partitionists. The Fermanagh Herald prints the uncontested nominations. Unionist recapture of a seat lost three years before. Printed as 'Mullynagoan' in 1949 and 'Mullynagowan' in 1952."
